                <pb facs="0432" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg352"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Squiers</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June 13,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that the Department has been advised that a Ward Line steamer is
                    detained at Habana with Chinese, and instructs Mr. Squiers to suggest to Cuban
                    Government that it would be reasonable not to consider exclusion provision
                    enforceable against vessels arriving upon voyages begun before promulgation of
                    the law excluding Chinese from Cuba.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
